# author : Y. Sharma
# date_created : 2025-10-20
# status : draft
# type : echelle:table
# min_wave_unit : nm
# max_wave_unit : nm
# echelle_blaze_unit : deg
# focal_length_unit : mm
# collimator1_focal_length_unit : mm
# collimator2_focal_length_unit : mm
# entrance_slit_scale_unit : mm/arcsec
# dispersion_focal_length_unit : mm
# fwhm_unit : pixel
# nominal_slit_width_unit : arcsec
# plate_scale_unit : arcsec/mm
# detector_pad_unit : pixel
# pixel_size_unit : mm
# n_disp_unit : pixel
# n_xdisp_unit : pixel
# disp_freq_unit : mm
# xdisp_freq_unit : mm
# slitlength_unit : arcsec
# detector_angle_unit : deg
# detector_offset_x_unit : mm
# detector_offset_y_unit : mm
# description : Table that defines the parameters for the analytical echelle trace generator used by EchelleSpectralTraceList effect. m0 = maximum order number; n = number of orders
# geometry_note : The two collimators and entrance_slit_scale determine the slit angle and pupil relay. dispersion_focal_length=270 mm and fwhm=4.46 pixels record rounded derived nominal values; the trace generator calculates them from the physical inputs. plate_scale is the along-slit sky-to-image scale. detector_angle rotates the trace before fixed placement. detector_pad is legacy metadata and is not optical geometry.
# future_trace_note : These analytical consistency columns are not a replacement for future Zemax-export trace tables. Zemax-backed traces should carry their own image-plane geometry and validation metadata.
# prescription : 20260610B_ZS_6CH_Complete_Spectrograph.zar; echelle/CX rulings and order limits from surfaces 61/88. Nominal focal lengths and 15 um production detector pixels are retained.
# angle_note : xbeta_center is the explicit unfolded CX incidence/central angle, in degrees. For local propagation sign s, alpha = -s * surface-85 Tilt-X; s is negative for B/G/YJ/H and positive for R/K. detector_angle is the negative of surface-166 coordinate Tilt-Z because it actively rotates points rather than coordinate axes. Neither angle is fitted to detector coverage.
# placement_note : detector_offset_x/y locate the rotated analytical camera origin relative to detector center, positive right/up. These fixed positions preserve comparison row 2 with R shifted left 150 pixels, H left 130 pixels and YJ up 50 pixels; B/G/K are unchanged. They replace automatic centering, not offsets added after centering.
# yj_order_note : Temporarily exclude reddest YJ order 57 (approximately 1320-1343 nm FSR) for detector coverage; retain orders 58-80. Placement was fixed before removing this order so the retained orders do not recenter.
# changes :
# - 2025-10-20 : Initial creation of the file with trace parameters
#
